{"name":"Ninja Turtle","hex":"#94b1a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ninja","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One trained in ninjutsu, especially one used for espionage, assassination, and other tasks requiring stealth during Japan's shogunate period.","One who very skillful, considered similar to the historical ninja, especially in covert or stealthy operation."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fast and sneaky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ninja"},{"term":"turtle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any land, aquatic, or semi-aquatic reptile of the order Testudines, characterised by a protective shell enclosing its body. See also tortoise.","A marine reptile of that order."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flip over onto the back or top; to turn upside down.\n\nTo turn and swim upside down.\n\n To capsize, turning fully over.","To turn and swim upside down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turtle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles","blocks":[{"text":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles (TMNT) is an American media franchise created by comic book artists Kevin Eastman and Peter Laird. It follows Leonardo, Donatello, Raphael and Michelangelo, four anthropomorphic turtle brothers trained in ninjutsu who fight evil in New York City. The franchise encompasses printed media, television series, feature films, video games, and merchandise."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teenage_Mutant_Ninja_Turtles","wikidata":"Q1381762"},{"title":"Ninja","blocks":[{"text":"A ninja , shinobi no mono  or shinobi  was a spy and infiltrator in pre-modern Japan. Antecedents may have existed as early as the 12th century. Despite popular belief, there is little evidence that ninja were assassins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Hokusai-sketches---hokusai-manga-vol6-crop.jpg/330px-Hokusai-sketches---hokusai-manga-vol6-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninja","wikidata":"Q9402"},{"title":"Turtle","blocks":[{"text":"Turtles are reptiles characterized by a special shell developed mainly from their ribs. Modern turtles are divided into two major groups, the Pleurodira and Cryptodira, which differ in the way the head retracts. There are 360 living and recently extinct species of turtles, including land-dwelling tortoises and freshwater terrapins. They are found on most continents, some islands and, in the case of sea turtles, much of the ocean. Like other amniotes they breathe air and do not lay eggs underwater, although many species live in or around water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Turtle_diversity.jpg/330px-Turtle_diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle","wikidata":"Q223044"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Kevin_Eastman.jpg/500px-Kevin_Eastman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Kevin_Eastman.jpg/500px-Kevin_Eastman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKevin_Eastman.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/4.20.08PeterLairdByLuigiNovi.JPG/500px-4.20.08PeterLairdByLuigiNovi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/4.20.08PeterLairdByLuigiNovi.JPG/1280px-4.20.08PeterLairdByLuigiNovi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/4.20.08PeterLairdByLuigiNovi.JPG/500px-4.20.08PeterLairdByLuigiNovi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars